00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:12.640
FATIMA: Hello.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:15.640
I'm Fatima [INAUDIBLE],, a system
engineer with the Google Cloud

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:16.990
Cortex team.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:19.570
And if you're interested in
learning about the Cortex

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:22.000
Application Layer, then
this video is for you.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.540
The Cortex Application Layer can
be used as a blueprint for you

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.460
to view the distributed
and scalable

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.310
applications to securely
consume information

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:34.570
from the Cortex Data Foundation
content residing in BigQuery,

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:37.720
our scalable data
cloud warehouse.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:39.760
It is composed of the
following services

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:43.968
and provides you a blueprint
to get started quickly.

00:00:43.968 --> 00:00:45.760
An event-driven
architecture using Pub/Sub;

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:47.920
an event source--

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:50.230
this is usually your
system of record.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:53.575
For demonstration, we are using
Cloud Scheduler; a controller

00:00:53.575 --> 00:00:54.550
service--

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:58.740
in this case, an inventory
to query inventory levels;

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:02.300
a data access layer that will
securely access BigQuery;

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:05.690
an output service to publish
the results for your query

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:07.870
to Pub/Sub.

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:09.340
The blueprint
provided allows you

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:11.380
to easily add
other microservices

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:14.290
with additional functionality
and reuse the secure data

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:17.440
access and output
patterns created.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:20.560
For example, you could
use a synchronous call

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:23.050
to complement master
data when creating it

00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:27.040
in the system of record, like
SAP, or publish a message

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:29.350
about new stock requirements
for your different

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:32.907
demanding planning systems
to subscribe and consume.

00:01:32.907 --> 00:01:34.990
You can deploy the Cortex
Application Layer sample

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:36.970
content from the Marketplace.

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:39.310
For quick access, navigate
through the Cortex App

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:41.210
through the link on the screen.

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:43.400
Now let's see this in action.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:46.050
First, we navigate to
the Marketplace page.

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:47.690
However, before
the point, you need

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:49.910
to complete the setup
instructions outlined

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:52.160
on the Deployment
Instructions Guide.

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:53.960
This guide has the
comprehensive steps

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:56.120
to configure your environment.

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:58.400
At the end of this guide,
you have all the information

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.260
you need in order to
deploy the application

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:02.390
content in your project.

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:04.170
I have already
completed these steps

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:07.250
and this is the output of the
last step in the compilation.

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:09.229
We are ready to deploy.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:11.030
Let's go ahead and
click on Configure

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:14.510
and start populating our fields
with the correct parameters.

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:16.805
Simply copy the fields
in the correct place.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:27.900
For the reporting
data set, this should

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:31.170
be the name of the data set
where you deployed the Cortex

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:34.380
data formation models,
which in this example

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:37.830
is the same project with
the name UnicornReporting.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:43.330
Complete the remaining fields.

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:53.830
When ready, click Deploy.

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:56.590
At this stage, the application
is creating the components

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:58.690
we saw in the diagram earlier.

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:01.240
In addition, as part
of the deployments,

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:03.130
the sample code for
this application

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:06.145
is added to the cloud
source repository for you

00:03:06.145 --> 00:03:08.170
to browse and modify.

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:10.720
Check the Readme for a detailed
breakdown of components

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:13.680
